---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /brand.html
title: "Monogram options — for review"
description: "Three ZT monogram options for Zachery Taylor's site, shown at favicon, navigation, and large sizes on light and dark backgrounds."
sheet: B-001
sheetTitle: "Brand — monogram options"
noSitemap: true
noindex: true
options:
  - key: a
    name: "A · Title block"
    note: "Z and T share one top stroke, set inside a blueprint sheet frame with a title-block strip — the drawing-set motif used across the site."
  - key: b
    name: "B · Serif ligature"
    note: "Instrument Serif Z overlapped by an italic blueprint-blue T, on paper with a bronze rule. The most literary of the three — leans toward the book."
  - key: c
    name: "C · Benchmark"
    note: "A survey benchmark disk: graduated ring, section-marker circle split by a datum line, ZT above and a benchmark triangle below. The most ‘civil’."
---
{%- import "macros.njk" as ui with context -%}
<style>
  .mono-grid { display: grid; gap: 28px; }
  .mono { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(255,255,255,.8); }
  .mono > div { padding: 26px; }
  .mono .info h2 { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .mono .info p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  .mono .current { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 10px; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--blueprint); color: #fff; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .swatch { display: grid; gap: 18px; align-content: start; }
  .swatch.light { background: var(--paper); }
  .swatch.dark { background: #0f1419; color: #f3f0e8; }
  .swatch .k { font-size: .66rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .75; }
  .big svg { width: 168px; height: 168px; }
  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .tab { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 7px 12px; border-radius: 9px 9px 0 0; background: #fff; color: #333; font-size: .78rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.08); }
  .dark .tab { background: #262c33; color: #ddd; }
  .tab svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .fav32 svg { width: 32px; height: 32px; }
  .navmock { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: .95rem; }
  .navmock svg { width: 30px; height: 30px; }
  .navmock small { display: block; font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .7; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .mono { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
<header class="page-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ ui.sectionLabel("B-001", "For review") }}
    <h1>Monogram <em>options.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">Three directions for the ZT mark, each shown as a browser-tab favicon, at navigation size, and large — on paper and on ink. Option {{ site.monogram | upper }} is live in the nav, footer, and favicons right now. To switch, change <code>monogram: "{{ site.monogram }}"</code> in <code>site.config.js</code> to <code>"a"</code>, <code>"b"</code>, or <code>"c"</code>.</p>
  </div>
</header>
<section class="band" aria-label="Options">
  <div class="wrap mono-grid">
    {%- for o in options %}
    <article class="mono" aria-labelledby="opt-{{ o.key }}">
      <div class="info">
        {%- if o.key == site.monogram %}<span class="current">IN USE</span>{% endif %}
        <h2 id="opt-{{ o.key }}">{{ o.name }}</h2>
        <p>{{ o.note }}</p>
        <p style="margin-top:14px"><a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}.svg">Download SVG</a></p>
      </div>
      {%- for tone in ["light", "dark"] %}
      <div class="swatch {{ tone }}">
        <span class="k">{{ "On paper" if tone == "light" else "On ink" }}</span>
        <div class="row"><span class="tab">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }} Zachery Taylor</span><span class="fav32">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}</span></div>
        <span class="navmock">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}<span>Zachery Taylor<small>Civil Designer · EI</small></span></span>
        <div class="big">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}</div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
